% A `:- class` equation that calls a `requiring`-bounded function.
%
% Each (equation x signature) attempt of a class function is checked in
% a throwaway sub-session, which is handed the declaration facts rather
% than re-deriving them. A bounded function contributes *two* facts —
% its signature and its bounds — that share type variables, and the
% discharge only lands at the call's instantiation if that sharing
% survives the trip. Freshen the two facts independently and the bound
% is left at a variable nothing binds, so it stays residual and
% succeeds silently instead of failing.
%
% Both signatures below are chosen so that no `gt` can satisfy the
% bound: the equation must therefore fit neither, and report one
% NoMatchingOverload. If the sharing is lost, both attempts pass and
% nothing is reported at all.
:- module(typecheck_class_bounded_call, [result/1]).
:- use_module(library(prelude)).

:- chr_type colour ---> red ; green.

:- chr_constraint result(colour).

:- function (gt(int, int) -> bool).
gt(X, Y) -> X > Y.

:- function pick(T, T) -> T requiring gt(T, T) -> bool.
pick(X, _) -> X.

:- class (both(colour, colour) -> colour), (both(string, string) -> string).
both(X, Y) -> pick(X, Y).

go @ result(R) <=> R = both(red, green).
